A quick grep of the source implies that that indicates corruption in the
high score table (which it's reading in order to generate a
player-monster, by the look of things; the timing with the magic whistle
was coincidental).

NAO's high score table has been acting very weirdly recently (players
with low scores ending up high up the list), which is consistent with
the theory of high score corruption.

In other words, it's probably not anything to do with your game in
particular, but rather something weird to do with NAO's high score
table. I don't know how the table became corrupted, but it should be
safe to continue. (Your game might be slightly easier as a result;
reading the source implies that it substitutes a human mummy rather than
a player-monster in that situation, making your opposition considerably
less powerful.)

